There is a $7\times7$ grid, with one coin in the cell in the first row from the top and the fourth column from the left. A cell $Y$ is said to be diagonally below and to the left of a cell $X$ if, for some positive integer $k$, it is $k$ cells to the left and $k$ cells below $X$. Similarly, $Y$ is diagonally below and to the right of $X$ if, for some positive integer $k$, it is $k$ cells to the right and $k$ cells below $X$. For a cell $X$ not in the bottom row that contains a coin, any one of the following four operations may be performed:

(a) Remove the coin from $X$ and put one coin in the cell immediately below $X$.

(b) Remove the coin from $X$ and put one coin in each cell diagonally below and to the left of $X$.

(c) Remove the coin from $X$ and put one coin in each cell diagonally below and to the right of $X$.

(d) Remove the coin from $X$ and put one coin in the cell one place to the left and one place below $X$, and one coin in the cell one place to the right and one place below $X$. If only one of these cells exists, put a coin only in that cell.

If a cell in which a coin is to be placed already contains a coin, no coin is placed in that cell. Find the greatest possible number of coins on the grid after performing these operations some number of times.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(650);
for(int panel=0;panel<4;++panel) {
  pair offset=(8.5*panel,0);
  for(int j=0;j<=7;++j) {
    draw(offset+(j,0)--offset+(j,7),gray(0.55)+linewidth(0.3));
    draw(offset+(0,j)--offset+(7,j),gray(0.55)+linewidth(0.3));
  }
  pair s=offset+(3.5,6.5);
  draw(circle(s,0.20),dotted);
  pair[] destinations;
  if(panel==0) destinations.push(offset+(3.5,5.5));
  if(panel==1) for(int k=1;k<=3;++k) destinations.push(s+(-k,-k));
  if(panel==2) for(int k=1;k<=3;++k) destinations.push(s+(k,-k));
  if(panel==3) { destinations.push(s+(-1,-1));destinations.push(s+(1,-1)); }
  for(pair d:destinations) {
    pair shift=panel==1 ? (-0.25,0.3) : (panel==2 ? (0.25,0.3) : (0,0));
    draw((s+(0,-0.20))..((s+d)/2+shift)..(d+(0,0.20)),Arrow(4));
    fill(circle(d,0.20),black);
  }
  string[] names={"(a)","(b)","(c)","(d)"};
  label(names[panel],offset+(3.5,-0.7));
}
[/asy]
